  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Alert core support 2018-2021 - Core Support International Alert 2018-2021</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">International Alert k&#xE4;rnst&#xF6;d 2018-2021</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Alert is an independent peacebuilding non-governmental organisation with a global mission to work with people in conflict-affected and -threatened areas to make a positive difference for peace; to improve the substance and implementation of international policies relevant to peacebuilding; and to strengthen the peacebuilding sector, with a key focus on gender, prevention of violent extremism and economic development for peace. Its main methods of engagement include bringing people together through dialogue; capacity building through trainings, accompaniment (which involves offering continuous guidance and advice to people, organisations and companies as they build peace or operate in high-risk places) and undertaking policy research and advocacy. With Headquarters in London, United Kingdom, Alert is active in 27 countries and territories across all continents.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">International Alert &#xE4;r en oberoende och icke-statlig organisation med globalt fredsbyggande uppdrag att arbeta med m&#xE4;nniskor i konflikt-drabbade och -hotade omr&#xE5;den f&#xF6;r att ha en positiv inverkan f&#xF6;r fred, att st&#xE4;rka grunden och implementeringen av internationella policies som &#xE4;r relevanta f&#xF6;r fredsbyggande, och att st&#xE4;rka den fredsbyggande sektor, med ett tydligt fokus p&#xE5; j&#xE4;mst&#xE4;lldhet, f&#xF6;rebyggande av v&#xE5;ldsam extremism och ekonomisk utveckling f&#xF6;r fred. Dess huvudsakliga arbetss&#xE4;tt &#xE4;r att f&#xF6;ra m&#xE4;nniskor samman via dialog, kapacitetsutveckling via utbildningar, medf&#xF6;ljande (vilket inneb&#xE4;r att ge l&#xF6;pande v&#xE4;gledning och r&#xE5;d till m&#xE4;nniskor, organisationer och f&#xF6;retag n&#xE4;r de bygger fred eller verkar i h&#xF6;griskomr&#xE5;den) och att genomf&#xF6;ra policyforskning och p&#xE5;verkansarbete. Alert har huvudkontor i London, Storbritannien och &#xE4;r aktiv i 27 l&#xE4;nder och omr&#xE5;den &#xF6;ver alla kontinenter.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objectives&#xA0;of the intervention&#xA0;are shown below. This is the mission statement of International Alert, which informs the Strategic Perspective 2015-2019 and which will guide the new strategy from 2020.&#xA0;The overall objectives are:
1.) to work with people in conflict-affected and -threatened areas to make a positive difference for peace
2.) to improve the substance and implementation of international policies relevant to peacebuilding
3.) to strengthen the peacebuilding sector.
Based on this, the Strategic Perspective outlines six Pathways: Relations within and between communities (1); State-Citizen Relations (2); Gender relations (3); Crime, violence and instability (CVI) (4); Natural Resource Management and Climate Change (5); and Economic development for peace (6). Each pathway has a specific set of expected results, which guides&#xA0;all work of Alert. A country or regional programme may contribute to one or several of the pathways.</narrative>
  </description>
